{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-160402-r4541031","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Hyderabadi Fried Bread with Syrup and Nuts (Double ka meetha)","sourcePageId":160402,"sourceRevision":"4541031","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-04T22:06:23Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Hyderabadi%20Fried%20Bread%20with%20Syrup%20and%20Nuts%20(Double%20ka%20meetha)&oldid=4541031","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:05:28.092Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Pan fried recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments","Category:Recipes using almond","Category:Recipes using bread","Category:Recipes using cardamom","Category:Recipes using cashew","Category:Recipes using milk","Category:Recipes using nuts and seeds","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:South Indian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"29fa3f5d8b6c4b9ad0e212e3304338ce7c2bc7e9633d2135cc5d9a9d5df0bbb8","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| Category = Indian recipes\n| Rating = 3\n| Difficulty = 2\n| Image = [[Image:DoubleKaMeetha.JPG|300px]]\n}}\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Asian Cuisine|South Asian cuisines]] | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of India|Indian Cuisine]]\n\n'''Double ka meetha''' is a popular [[Cookbook:Dessert|dessert]] in [[w:Hyderabad|Hyderabad]], [[w:India|India]].\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 1 loaf [[Cookbook:Bread|bread]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Liter|litre]] [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]]\n* 250 [[Cookbook:Gram|grams]] [[Cookbook:Khoa|khoa]] (concentrated [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]] solids)\n* 500 grams [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 100 grams [[Cookbook:Almond|almond]]<nowiki/>s\n* 100 grams [[Cookbook:Cashew|cashews]]\n* 100 grams [[Cookbook:Pistachio|pistachios]]\n* 100 grams [[Cookbook:Raisin|raisins]]\n* 250 grams [[Cookbook:Ghee|ghee]]\n* 10 grams [[Cookbook:Cardamom|cardamom]]\n* 500 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n\n==Procedure==\n# Trim the edges of the bread slices and cut each slice into four.\n# [[Cookbook:Fry|Fry]] them in ghee till golden brown.\n# Make a sugar [[Cookbook:Syrup|syrup]] by adding half a litre of water to the sugar. Add the milk to the sugar syrup. [[Cookbook:Boil|Boil]] until the syrup starts thickening.\n# Grind the cardamom seeds to a powder.\n# Add the powdered cardamom seeds and khoa to the thickened milk. Stir the mixture well.\n# Arrange the fried bread pieces on a flat tray. Pour the syrup over the bread pieces while they are still hot. Garnish with the raisins and nuts.\n# Refrigerate and serve.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using bread]]\n[[Category:Recipes using milk]]\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using nuts and seeds]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments]]\n[[Category:Pan fried recipes]]\n[[Category:Indian recipes|Double ka Meetha]]\n[[Category:South Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using almond]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cardamom]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cashew]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Hyderabadi Fried Bread with Syrup and Nuts (Double ka meetha)","nameAr":nu